## Exact projection snapshots and cache

`meridian.evidence_serialization` provides exact closed mapping conversion for
the typed evidence inventory. `meridian.projection_cache` binds one validated
inventory to exact Core source state, adapter and reader identity, projection
authorization purpose and scope, canonical JSON, a deterministic cache key, and
a content digest.

Cache creation repeats canonical verification and authorization after adapter
work. Exact replay preserves original bytes and capture time. A different output
under identical declared inputs fails as projection nondeterminism. Public cache
reads require fresh authorization before opening student-level snapshot bytes.
Current assessment distinguishes reusable, reprojection-required, historical,
and unverifiable states without rewriting historical snapshots.

These projection snapshots are derived cache entries, not report snapshots,
Grades, proficiency results, or mutable current views. See
[`docs/architecture/exact-projection-snapshots-and-cache.md`](docs/architecture/exact-projection-snapshots-and-cache.md).
